INFO:agent.loop:\u26a1 Executing tool: 'knowledge_agent' with arguments: {"source_title": "Mandiant / Google Cloud: 3CX Software Supply Chain Compromise", "source_url": "https://cloud.google.com/blog/topics/threat-intelligence/3cx-software-supply-chain-compromise", "text": "SRC-003 reports Mandiant identified the initial compromise vector of 3CX's network as malicious software downloaded from the Trading Technologies website: a prior supply-chain compromise involving a tampered X_TRADER installer. A 3CX employee installed the infected X_TRADER package, enabling attacker access and lateral movement. Mandiant reconstructed credential harvesting and lateral movement, followed by compromise of both Windows and macOS build environments. On Windows, TAXHAUL and COLDCAT persisted via IKEEXT DLL search-order hijacking with LocalSystem privileges; on macOS, POOLRAT persisted through Launch Daemons. The attacker then compromised the 3CX build environment and trojanized 3CX DesktopApp installers. Affected 3CX DesktopApp 18.12.416 and earlier contained SUDDENICON, which used encrypted icon files hosted on GitHub to obtain C2 servers, then downloaded ICONICSTEALER, which stole browser information. Mandiant tracks activity as UNC4736, a suspected North Korean nexus cluster, and assesses with moderate confidence that UNC4736 is related to financially motivated North Korean AppleJeus activity. It cites POOLRAT overlap with a sample used in the trojanized CoinGoTrade AppleJeus operation and infrastructure ties to JMT Trading. Mandiant notes weak infrastructure overlap with suspected APT43 clusters UNC3782 and UNC4469, but does not present that as primary attribution."}
